Third-party data
----------------
The EUPL covers the code and documentation in this repository. These data
files in Karlstad's municipality profile keep their own terms:

next/src/caia/kommuner/karlstad/data/Kommunrapport_karlstad_vaxthusgaser_totalt.csv
  Source: SMHI, Nationella emissionsdatabasen (data from SMED, commissioned
  by Naturvårdsverket), county report 2025-04-04. Licence: CC BY 4.0.
  Changed: the Swedish letters å, ä and ö in the labels are replaced by the
  replacement character U+FFFD; CAIA repairs the labels when it reads the
  file. The figures are unchanged.

next/src/caia/kommuner/karlstad/data/energianvandning_bostader_karlstad.csv
  Source: SCB, Kommunal och regional energistatistik, table EN0203A, 2022
  (rows Småhus, Flerbostadshus, Fritidshus). Licence: CC0. The rows Totalt
  and Per person are calculated by Karlstads kommun.

The parameter library (parameters_library.md) quotes individual figures from
Resvaneundersökning Region Värmland 2023, municipal report Karlstad (Region
Värmland and Enkätfabriken), with figure and page for each. The report
itself is not included.

Karlstads kommun's own data
---------------------------
The municipal group's consumption-based emissions 2022
(Kommunkoncernens_egna_konsumtionsbaserade_CO2e-utsläpp.json, calculated by
Svalna on the municipality's commission, also quoted in docs/METOD.md and
potter.toml) and the citizen survey 2024 (medborgarundersokning_karlstad_2024.csv,
also quoted in the exempel profile) are the municipality's own data, released
with the code under the EUPL.

Not included
------------
Karlstad's installation also reads five files from Konsumtionskompassen
(Stockholm Environment Institute), licensed CC BY-NC-ND 4.0, which cannot be
distributed under the EUPL. Without them the profile's CONS_* rows use their
standard values. A municipality that wants consumption-based data exports its
own from https://konsumtionskompassen.se/ and cites it as "Stockholm
Environment Institute (SEI), Konsumtionskompassen, 2025".
